From 696d604637ee39b6812cbf0024cfb884d8cc0f7d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Stephano Cetola <stephano@cetola.net>
Date: Thu, 9 Jul 2026 18:47:57 +0000
Subject: input: usb_kbd_hid: seed idle baseline to fix spurious keypress at
 connect

data->old is zeroed by xzalloc. usb_kbd_poll() detects keypresses by
diffing data->new against data->old, so the first real report seen
after probe gets diffed against that zeroed state instead of against
the device's actual idle state. This keyboard's first report contains
nonzero bytes even when no key is pressed (observed: 01 03 44 00 45
00 36 00), which read against a zeroed baseline as a fresh keypress:
0x36 (HID comma) at byte [6] came out as KEY_COMMA permanently
pressed, auto-repeat flooding the barebox prompt.

Fix by copying the first captured report into data->old before
registering the poller, so only real transitions from that point on
produce key events.

Also request report protocol (1) instead of boot protocol (0) in
SET_PROTOCOL. The keyboard's HID interface descriptor declares
HID_ITF_PROTOCOL_NONE (pocket-reform-keyboard-fw usb_descriptors.c),
so it was never a boot-protocol-compatible device to begin with, and
its firmware sends the same Report-ID-prefixed layout regardless of
the negotiated protocol (main.c always calls
tud_hid_keyboard_report(REPORT_ID_KEYBOARD, ...) unconditionally).
Requesting boot protocol was a mismatched request the device happened
to accept without complaint. This keeps the request consistent with
what the device actually declares and sends.

Scan the full [3:7] keycode window in the key-released loop instead
of stopping at the first zero byte. This keyboard's firmware compacts
pressed keycodes to the front of the report and zero-pads the rest,
so the two are normally equivalent, but scanning unconditionally
removes the driver's dependency on that packing behavior holding for
every report.

Signed-off-by: Stephano Cetola <stephano@cetola.net>
---
 drivers/input/usb_kbd_hid.c | 9 ++++++---
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/input/usb_kbd_hid.c b/drivers/input/usb_kbd_hid.c
index 52c11b61bf..5b41be4dc8 100644
--- a/drivers/input/usb_kbd_hid.c
+++ b/drivers/input/usb_kbd_hid.c
@@ -157,8 +157,6 @@ static void usb_kbd_poll(void *arg)
 			if (gone) {
 				input_report_key_event(&data->input, usb_kbd_keycode[pressed_old], 0);
 			}
-		} else {
-			break;
 		}
 	}
 
@@ -176,7 +174,8 @@ static int usb_kbd_probe(struct usb_device *usbdev,
 	struct usb_kbd_pdata *data;
 
 	dev_info(&usbdev->dev, "USB HID keyboard found\n");
-	ret = usb_set_protocol(usbdev, iface->desc.bInterfaceNumber, 0);
+	/* Report protocol matches what this device's descriptor declares. */
+	ret = usb_set_protocol(usbdev, iface->desc.bInterfaceNumber, 1);
 	if (ret < 0)
 		return ret;
 
@@ -214,6 +213,10 @@ static int usb_kbd_probe(struct usb_device *usbdev,
 	} else
 		dev_info(&usbdev->dev, "poll keyboard via int ep\n");
 
+	/* data->old starts zeroed; seed it from the real idle report so the
+	 * first poll doesn't read nonzero idle bytes as a keypress. */
+	memcpy(data->old, data->new, USB_KBD_BOOT_REPORT_SIZE);
+
 	data->input.parent = &usbdev->dev;
 	ret = input_device_register(&data->input);
 	if (ret) {
